## Original Content
Berlin entend doter son armée d’un arsenal de frappe à longue portée pour faire face à la menace russe aux frontières de l’Otan, selon des documents secret défense consultés par le média américain Politico.

## Summary
Germany is planning a €12 billion defense investment to acquire long-range weapons like cruise missiles and hypersonic gliders with ranges over 2000 km. This initiative aims to deter Russian threats at NATO's borders, based on classified documents reported by Politico.

## Key Points
- Germany plans a €12 billion defense investment.
- Acquisition includes cruise missiles and hypersonic gliders.
- Weapons have a range exceeding 2000 kilometers.
- Goal is to deter Russian aggression near NATO borders.
- Information sourced from classified documents consulted by Politico.


